      <p>Common questions about biomimetic dentistry and Dr. Noot's practice:</p>
    </div>
    
    <div class="grid grid-2">
      <div>
        <h4>What is biomimetic dentistry?</h4>
        <p>Biomimetic dentistry mimics the natural properties of teeth using advanced materials and techniques. It preserves your natural tooth structure instead of destroying it like traditional crowns.</p>
        
        <h4>Does Dr. Noot accept insurance?</h4>
        <p>We work with most dental insurance plans. Our office will help verify your benefits and maximize your coverage for biomimetic treatments.</p>
        
        <h4>How long do biomimetic restorations last?</h4>
        <p>When properly executed, biomimetic restorations can last your entire lifetime because they preserve and strengthen your natural tooth structure.</p>
      </div>
      
      <div>
        <h4>Are biomimetic treatments painful?</h4>
        <p>Dr. Noot's advanced techniques often eliminate the need for needles and drills, making treatment much more comfortable than traditional dentistry.</p>
        
        <h4>How is this different from regular dental work?</h4>
        <p>Traditional dentistry removes healthy tooth structure to fit crowns. Biomimetic dentistry preserves healthy structure and creates restorations that strengthen your natural teeth.</p>
        
        <h4>Do you treat dental emergencies?</h4>
        <p>Yes, Dr. Noot provides emergency dental care for patients. Call our office and we'll arrange prompt treatment to address your urgent dental needs.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

